Role-Based Wedding Day Micro-Checklists — Template pages (one role per page)

Page header: Role: {ROLE_NAME}
Subtitle: Date: {WEDDING_DATE} | Venue: {VENUE}

Section 1 — 24 hrs before
- Confirm final vendor arrival times
- Pack emergency kit (band-aids, safety pins, stain remover, pain relief)
- Confirm contact numbers for: coordinator, vendors, transport
- Charge phones & portable battery
- Confirm who has the rings
- Final weather check & alternate plan note

Section 2 — Morning
- Wake-up time: ______
- Breakfast for role & support (note food allergies)
- Assigned hair/makeup times (if applicable)
- Final outfit check (dress/suit, shoes, accessories)
- Personal essentials packed: ID, cash/cards, meds

Section 3 — At ceremony
- Where to stand / procession cue & timing
- Key contacts to check in with (name + mobile)
- Quick role-specific duties (e.g., hold bouquet, adjust veil, cue readings)
- Emergency plan (who escorts whom if late)

Section 4 — Vendor handoff & immediate post-ceremony
- Photographer cue items (specific shots requested)
- Reception contacts & timing note
- Items to return/collect (decor, signage)
- Where to leave personal items for safe-keeping

Footer: Notes / Additional contacts
- Name: ___________ Role: ___________ Phone: ___________
- Quick checklist of final confirmations: [ ] Rings with: ______  [ ] Marriage license with: ______

Design & layout notes: keep each section clearly boxed with heading, 6–10 checklist lines per section, checkboxes left-aligned, and a small contact block at the bottom. Leave blank lines for handwritten notes.